  You composed this core idea first — DEVELOP it, never replace it. Form: gat.
  Energy arc: Intro (Alaap): 2/10 - Somber, unmetered resonance dwelling in the mandra register over tanpura. Mukhada: 5/10 - Crushing doom rhythm locks to the Masitkhani pulse with low-octave weight. Manjha: 4/10 - Dark drop into the subterranean depths, lingering around mandra Pa and dha. Returning Mukhada: 6/10 - Re-entry of the head with amplified conviction and rhythmic bite. Antara: 7/10 - Stately melodic climb towards taar Sa, building immense emotional tension. Taan Long: 9/10 - Climax of rapid sitar virtuosity driven relentlessly over a massive Sa pedal. Outro: 3/10 - Slow decay of the final root note into feedback and subterranean drone.
  The gat HEAD'S IDEA (the mukhada is composed FROM it — land its sam swara; the motif and the stroke line are yours):
    idea: Masitkhani vilambit gat in Darbari Kanada. Start from WEIGHT: open low (the mandra or the lower madhya), give komal Ga and komal Dha long holds where they rest so they sway, and let the head move slowly and gravely, like an alap set in time; the metal weight comes from the band underneath.
